# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
config RUST_KTHREAD
	bool "Rust kernel thread lifecycle and worker implementation"
	depends on RUST
	default y
	help
	  Select Rust as the production owner of kernel/kthread.o. All task
	  creation, park/stop, affinity, worker queue/cancel/flush, address-space
	  switching and block-cgroup association bodies are implemented in Rust
	  using configured native layouts. The original C source is retained
	  for reference and explicit control comparisons.

	  The source retains NUMA, FREEZER, BLK_CGROUP, PREEMPT_RT, lockdep and
	  debug/list behavior. Native compiler, instrumentation, configuration
	  and runtime qualification is still pending; these profiles have not
	  all been validated. The integrated production target must keep this
	  selector enabled and resolve qualification failures explicitly, without
	  silently falling back to the C implementation.
